ngID for MFA","path":"v1.21.x/enterprise/mfa/mfa-pingid","fullPath":"/vault/docs/v1.21.x/enterprise/mfa/mfa-pingid","id":"sidebar-nav-item-729"},{"title":"Configure TOTP for MFA","path":"v1.21.x/enterprise/mfa/mfa-totp","fullPath":"/vault/docs/v1.21.x/enterprise/mfa/mfa-totp","id":"sidebar-nav-item-730"}],"id":"sidebar-nav-item-725"},{"title":"Manage policies as code","routes":[{"title":"Manage Vault policies with Sentinel","path":"v1.21.x/enterprise/sentinel","fullPath":"/vault/docs/v1.21.x/enterprise/sentinel","id":"sidebar-nav-item-732"},{"title":"Sentinel properties for Vault","path":"v1.21.x/enterprise/sentinel/properties","fullPath":"/vault/docs/v1.21.x/enterprise/sentinel/properties","id":"sidebar-nav-item-733"},{"title":"Sentinel examples","path":"v1.21.x/enterprise/sentinel/examples","fullPath":"/vault/docs/v1.21.x/enterprise/sentinel/examples","id":"sidebar-nav-item-734"}],"id":"sidebar-nav-item-731"},{"title":"HCP Vault docs","href":"/hcp/docs/vault","id":"sidebar-nav-item-735"}],"id":"sidebar-nav-item-685"},{"divider":true,"id":"sidebar-nav-item-736"},{"title":"Glossary","path":"v1.21.x/glossary","fullPath":"/vault/docs/v1.21.x/glossary","id":"sidebar-nav-item-737"}],"title":"Documentation","visuallyHideTitle":true}],"mainWidth":"narrow","githubFileUrl":"https://github.com/hashicorp/web-unified-docs/blob/main/content/vault/v1.21.x/content/docs/auth/jwt/index.mdx"},"metadata":{"title":"Use JWT/OIDC authentication","description":"Use JWT/OIDC authentication with Vault to support OIDC and user-provided JWTs.","layout":null,"structuredData":{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"TechArticle","headline":"Use JWT/OIDC authentication","description":"Use JWT/OIDC authentication with Vault to support OIDC and user-provided JWTs.","url":"https://developer.hashicorp.comundefined","datePublished":"2025-07-22T19:58:23.000Z","dateModified":"2025-10-22T20:53:42.000Z","author":{"@type":"Organization","name":"HashiCorp","url":"https://www.hashicorp.com"},"publisher":{"@type":"Organization","name":"HashiCorp"},"isPartOf":{"@type":"WebSite","name":"HashiCorp Developer","url":"https://developer.hashicorp.com"},"about":{"@type":"SoftwareApplication","name":"Vault"}}},"outlineItems":[{"title":"Use JWT/OIDC authentication","url":"#use-jwt-oidc-authentication"},{"title":"OIDC authentication","url":"#oidc-authentication"},{"title":"JWT authentication","url":"#jwt-authentication"},{"title":"Configuration","url":"#configuration"},{"title":"Tutorial","url":"#tutorial"},{"title":"API","url":"#api"}],"pageHeading":{"id":"use-jwt-oidc-authentication","title":"Use JWT/OIDC authentication"},"mdxSource":{"compiledSource":"const makeShortcode=name=\u003efunction MDXDefaultShortcode(props){console.warn(\"Component \"+name+\" was not imported, exported, or provided by MDXProvider as global scope\");return mdx(\"div\",props)};const Note=makeShortcode(\"Note\");const Tip=makeShortcode(\"Tip\");const layoutProps={};const MDXLayout=\"wrapper\";function MDXContent({components,...props}){return mdx(MDXLayout,{...layoutProps,...props,components:components,mdxType:\"MDXLayout\"},mdx(Note,{mdxType:\"Note\"},mdx(\"p\",null,`This engine can use external X.509 certificates as part of TLS or signature validation.\nVerifying signatures against X.509 certificates that use SHA-1 is deprecated and is no longer\nusable without a workaround starting in Vault 1.12. Refer to the\n`,mdx(\"a\",{parentName:\"p\",\"href\":\"/vault/docs/v1.21.x/updates/deprecation\"},`deprecation notices`),`\nfor more information.`)),mdx(Tip,{title:\"Supports custom GUI login\",mdxType:\"Tip\"},mdx(\"p\",null,`This method can be chosen as a default or backup login method for Vault Enterprise GUI users.\nRefer to the `,mdx(\"a\",{parentName:\"p\",\"href\":\"/vault/docs/v1.21.x/ui/custom-login\"},`Manage custom login options`),` guide for more details. `)),mdx(\"div\",{className:\"alert alert-warning g-type-body\"},mdx(\"p\",null,mdx(\"strong\",{parentName:\"p\"},`Note`),`: Starting in Vault 1.17, if the JWT in the authentication request\ncontains an `,mdx(\"inlineCode\",{parentName:\"p\"},`aud`),` claim (typical case) the associated `,mdx(\"inlineCode\",{parentName:\"p\"},`bound_audiences`),` for the\n\"jwt\" role must `,mdx(\"strong\",{parentName:\"p\"},`exactly`),` match at least one of the `,mdx(\"inlineCode\",{parentName:\"p\"},`aud`),` claims declared for\nthe JWT. For\nadditional details, refer to the `,mdx(\"a\",{parentName:\"p\",\"href\":\"/vault/api-docs/v1.21.x/auth/jwt\"},`JWT auth method (API)`),`\ndocumentation and `,mdx(\"a\",{parentName:\"p\",\"href\":\"/vault/docs/v1.21.x/upgrading/upgrade-to-1.17.x#jwt-auth-login-requires-bound-audiences-on-the-role\"},`1.17 Upgrade Guide`),`.`)),mdx(\"p\",null,`The `,mdx(\"inlineCode\",{parentName:\"p\"},`jwt`),` auth method can be used to authenticate with Vault using\n`,mdx(\"a\",{parentName:\"p\",\"href\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/OpenID_Connect\"},`OIDC`),` or by providing a\n`,mdx(\"a\",{parentName:\"p\",\"href\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/JSON_Web_Token\"},`JWT`),`.`),mdx(\"p\",null,`The OIDC method allows authentication via a configured OIDC provider using the\nuser's web browser. This method may be initiated from the Vault UI or the\ncommand line. Alternatively, a JWT can be provided directly. The JWT is\ncryptographically verified using locally-provided keys, or, if configured, an\nOIDC Discovery service can be used to fetch the appropriate keys. The choice of\nmethod is configured per role.`),mdx(\"p\",null,`Both methods allow additional processing of the claims data in the JWT. Some of\nthe concepts common to both methods will be covered first, followed by specific\nexamples of OIDC and JWT usage.`),mdx(\"h2\",{\"id\":\"oidc-authentication\"},mdx(\"a\",{parentName:\"h2\",\"className\":\"__permalink-h\",\"href\":\"#oidc-authentication\",\"aria-label\":\"oidc authentication permalink\"},`\\xbb`),`OIDC authentication`),mdx(\"p\",null,`This section covers the setup and use of OIDC roles. If a JWT is to be provided directly,\nrefer to the `,mdx(\"a\",{parentName:\"p\",\"href\":\"/vault/docs/v1.21.x/auth/jwt#jwt-authentication\"},`JWT Authentication`),` section below. Basic\nfamiliarity with `,mdx(\"a\",{parentName:\"p\",\"href\":\"https://developer.okta.com/blog/2017/07/25/oidc-primer-part-1\"},`OIDC concepts`),`\nis assumed. The Authorization Code flow makes use of the Proof Key for Code\nExchange (PKCE) extension.`),mdx(\"p\",null,`Vault includes two built-in OIDC login flows: the Vault UI, and the CLI\nusing a `,mdx(\"inlineCode\",{parentName:\"p\"},`vault login`),`.`),mdx(\"h3\",{\"id\":\"redirect-uris\"},mdx(\"a\",{parentName:\"h3\",\"className\":\"__permalink-h\",\"href\":\"#redirect-uris\",\"aria-label\":\"redirect uris permalink\"},`\\xbb`),`Redirect URIs`),mdx(\"p\",null,`An important part of OIDC role configuration is properly setting redirect URIs. This must be\ndone both in Vault and with the OIDC provider, and these configurations must align. The\nredirect URIs are specified for a role with the `,mdx(\"inlineCode\",{parentName:\"p\"},`allowed_redirect_uris`),` parameter. There are\ndifferent redirect URIs to configure the Vault UI and CLI flows, so one or both will need to\nbe set up depending on the installation.`),mdx(\"p\",null,mdx(\"strong\",{parentName:\"p\"},`CLI`)),mdx(\"p\",null,`If you plan to support authentication via `,mdx(\"inlineCode\",{parentName:\"p\"},`vault login -method=oidc`),`, a localhost redirect URI\nmust be set. This can usually be: `,mdx(\"inlineCode\",{parentName:\"p\"},`http://localhost:8250/oidc/callback`),`. Logins via the CLI may\nspecify a different host and/or listening port if needed, and a URI with this host/port must match one\nof the configured redirected URIs. These same \"localhost\" URIs must be added to the provider as well.`),mdx(\"p\",null,mdx(\"strong\",{parentName:\"p\"},`Vault UI`)),mdx(\"p\",null,`Logging in via the Vault UI requires a redirect URI of the form:`),mdx(\"p\",null,mdx(\"inlineCode\",{parentName:\"p\"},`https://{host:port}/ui/vault/auth/{path}/oidc/callback`)),mdx(\"p\",null,`The \"host:port\" must be correct for the Vault server, and \"path\" must match the path the JWT\nbackend is mounted at (e.g. \"oidc\" or \"jwt\").`),mdx(\"p\",null,`If the `,mdx(\"a\",{parentName:\"p\",\"href\":\"/vault/api-docs/v1.21.x/auth/jwt#oidc_response_mode\"},`oidc_response_mode`),` is set to `,mdx(\"inlineCode\",{parentName:\"p\"},`form_post`),`, then\nlogging in via the Vault UI requires a redirect URI of the form:`),mdx(\"p\",null,mdx(\"inlineCode\",{parentName:\"p\"},`https://{host:port}/v1/auth/{path}/oidc/callback`)),mdx(\"p\",null,`Prior to Vault 1.6, if `,mdx(\"a\",{parentName:\"p\",\"href\":\"/vault/docs/v1.21.x/enterprise/namespaces\"},`namespaces`),` are in use,\nthey must be added as query parameters, for example:`),mdx(\"p\",null,mdx(\"inlineCode\",{parentName:\"p\"},`https://vault.example.com:8200/ui/vault/auth/oidc/oidc/callback?namespace=my_ns`)),mdx(\"p\",null,`For Vault 1.6+, it is no longer necessary to add the namespace as a query\nparameter in the redirect URI, if\n`,mdx(\"a\",{parentName:\"p\",\"href\":\"/vault/api-docs/v1.21.x/auth/jwt#namespace_in_state\"},mdx(\"inlineCode\",{parentName:\"a\"},`namespace_in_state`)),` is set to `,mdx(\"inlineCode\",{parentName:\"p\"},`true`),`,\nwhich is the default for new configs.`),mdx(\"h3\",{\"id\":\"oidc-login-vault-ui\"},mdx(\"a\",{parentName:\"h3\",\"className\":\"__permalink-h\",\"href\":\"#oidc-login-vault-ui\",\"aria-label\":\"oidc login vault ui permalink\"},`\\xbb`),`OIDC login (Vault UI)`),mdx(\"ol\",null,mdx(\"li\",{parentName:\"ol\"},`Select the \"OIDC\" login method.`),mdx(\"li\",{parentName:\"ol\"},`Enter a role name if necessary.`),mdx(\"li\",{parentName:\"ol\"},`Press \"Sign In\" and complete the authentication with the configured provider.`)),mdx(\"h3\",{\"id\":\"oidc-login-cli\"},mdx(\"a\",{parentName:\"h3\",\"className\":\"__permalink-h\",\"href\":\"#oidc-login-cli\",\"aria-label\":\"oidc login cli permalink\"},`\\xbb`),`OIDC login (CLI)`),mdx(\"p\",null,`The CLI login defaults to path of `,mdx(\"inlineCode\",{parentName:\"p\"},`/oidc`),`. If this auth method was enabled at a\ndifferent path, specify `,mdx(\"inlineCode\",{parentName:\"p\"},`-path=/my-path`),` in the CLI.`),mdx(\"pre\",{\"style\":{\"backgroundColor\":\"var(--code-block-color-surface-primary)\",\"color\":\"var(--code-block-color-token)\"},\"tabindex\":\"0\",\"language\":\"shellsession\",\"className\":\"language-shellsession\"},mdx(\"code\",{parentName:\"pre\",\"className\":\"language-shellsession\"},mdx(\"span\",{parentName:\"code\",\"className\":\"line\"},mdx(\"span\",{parentName:\"span\",\"style\":{\"color\":\"var(--code-block-color-cyan)\"}},`$`),mdx(\"span\",{parentName:\"span\",\"style\":{\"color\":\"var(--code-block-color-token)\"}},` vault login -method=oidc port=8400 role=test`)),`\n`,`\n`,mdx(\"span\",{parentName:\"code\",\"className\":\"line\"},mdx(\"span\",{parentName:\"span\",\"style\":{\"color\":\"var(--code-block-color-token)\"}},`Complete the login via your OIDC provider. Launching browser to:`)),`\n`,`\n`,mdx(\"span\",{parentName:\"code\",\"className\":\"line\"},mdx(\"span\",{parentName:\"span\",\"style\":{\"color\":\"var(--code-block-color-token)\"}},`    https://myco.auth0.com/authorize?redirect_uri=http%3A%2F%2Flocalhost%3A8400%2Foidc%2Fcallback\u0026client_id=r3qXc2bix9eF...`)),`\n`)),mdx(\"p\",null,`The browser will open to the generated URL to complete the provider's login. The\nURL may be entered manually if the browser cannot be automatically opened.`),mdx(\"ul\",null,mdx(\"li\",{parentName:\"ul\"},mdx(\"a\",{parentName:\"li\",\"id\":\"skip_browser\",\"className\":\"__target-lic\",\"aria-hidden\":\"true\"}),mdx(\"a\",{parentName:\"li\",\"href\":\"#skip_browser\",\"aria-label\":\"skip_browser permalink\",\"className\":\"__permalink-lic\"},mdx(\"inlineCode\",{parentName:\"a\"},`skip_browser`)),` (default: \"false\"). Toggle the automatic launching of the default browser to the login URL.`)),mdx(\"p\",null,`The callback listener may be customized with the following optional parameters. These are typically\nnot required to be set:`),mdx(\"ul\",null,mdx(\"li\",{parentName:\"ul\"},mdx(\"a\",{parentName:\"li\",\"id\":\"mount\",\"className\":\"__target-lic\",\"aria-hidden\":\"true\"}),mdx(\"a\",{parentName:\"li\",\"href\":\"#mount\",\"aria-label\":\"mount permalink\",\"className\":\"__permalink-lic\"},mdx(\"inlineCode\",{parentName:\"a\"},`mount`)),` (default: \"oidc\")`),mdx(\"li\",{parentName:\"ul\"},mdx(\"a\",{parentName:\"li\",\"id\":\"listenaddress\",\"className\":\"__target-lic\",\"aria-hidden\":\"true\"}),mdx(\"a\",{parentName:\"li\",\"href\":\"#listenaddress\",\"aria-label\":\"listenaddress permalink\",\"className\":\"__permalink-lic\"},mdx(\"inlineCode\",{parentName:\"a\"},`listenaddress`)),` (default: \"localhost\")`),mdx(\"li\",{parentName:\"ul\"},mdx(\"a\",{parentName:\"li\",\"id\":\"port\",\"className\":\"__target-lic\",\"aria-hidden\":\"true\"}),mdx(\"a\",{parentName:\"li\",\"href\":\"#port\",\"aria-label\":\"port permalink\",\"className\":\"__permalink-lic\"},mdx(\"inlineCode\",{parentName:\"a\"},`port`)),` (default: 8250)`),mdx(\"li\",{parentName:\"ul\"},mdx(\"a\",{parentName:\"li\",\"id\":\"callbackhost\",\"className\":\"__target-lic\",\"aria-hidden\":\"true\"}),mdx(\"a\",{parentName:\"li\",\"href\":\"#callbackhost\",\"aria-label\":\"callbackhost permalink\",\"className\":\"__permalink-lic\"},mdx(\"inlineCode\",{parentName:\"a\"},`callbackhost`)),` (default: \"localhost\")`),mdx(\"li\",{parentName:\"ul\"},mdx(\"a\",{parentName:\"li\",\"id\":\"callbackmethod\",\"className\":\"__target-lic\",\"aria-hidden\":\"true\"}),mdx(\"a\",{parentName:\"li\",\"href\":\"#callbackmethod\",\"aria-label\":\"callbackmethod permalink\",\"className\":\"__permalink-lic\"},mdx(\"inlineCode\",{parentName:\"a\"},`callbackmethod`)),` (default: \"http\")`),mdx(\"li\",{parentName:\"ul\"},mdx(\"a\",{parentName:\"li\",\"id\":\"callbackport\",\"className\":\"__target-lic\",\"aria-hidden\":\"true\"}),mdx(\"a\",{parentName:\"li\",\"href\":\"#callbackport\",\"aria-label\":\"callbackport permalink\",\"className\":\"__permalink-lic\"},mdx(\"inlineCode\",{parentName:\"a\"},`callbackport`)),` (default: value set for `,mdx(\"inlineCode\",{parentName:\"li\"},`port`),`). This value is used in the `,mdx(\"inlineCode\",{parentName:\"li\"},`redirect_uri`),`, whereas\n`,mdx(\"inlineCode\",{parentName:\"li\"},`port`),` is the localhost port that the listener is using. These two may be different in advanced setups.`)),mdx(\"h3\",{\"id\":\"oidc-provider-configuration\"},mdx(\"a\",{parentName:\"h3\",\"className\":\"__permalink-h\",\"href\":\"#oidc-provider-configuration\",\"aria-label\":\"oidc provider configuration permalink\"},`\\xbb`),`OIDC provider configuration`),mdx(\"p\",null,`The OIDC authentication flow has been successfully tested with a number of providers. A full\nguide to configuring OAuth/OIDC applications is beyond the scope of Vault documentation, but a\ncollection of provider configuration steps has been collected to help get started:\n`,mdx(\"a\",{parentName:\"p\",\"href\":\"/vault/docs/v1.21.x/auth/jwt/oidc-providers\"},`OIDC Provider Setup`)),mdx(\"h3\",{\"id\":\"oidc-configuration-troubleshooting\"},mdx(\"a\",{parentName:\"h3\",\"className\":\"__permalink-h\",\"href\":\"#oidc-configuration-troubleshooting\",\"aria-label\":\"oidc configuration troubleshooting permalink\"},`\\xbb`),`OIDC configuration troubleshooting`),mdx(\"p\",null,`This amount of configuration required for OIDC is relatively small, but it can be tricky to debug\nwhy things aren't working. Some tips for setting up OIDC:`),mdx(\"ul\",null,mdx(\"li\",{parentName:\"ul\"},`If a role parameter (e.g. `,mdx(\"inlineCode\",{parentName:\"li\"},`bound_claims`),`) requires a map value, it can't be set individually using\nthe Vault CLI. In these cases the best approach is to write the entire configuration as a single\nJSON object:`)),mdx(\"pre\",{\"style\":{\"backgroundColor\":\"var(--code-block-color-surface-primary)\",\"color\":\"var(--code-block-color-token)\"},\"tabindex\":\"0\",\"language\":\"text\",\"className\":\"language-text\"},mdx(\"code\",{parentName:\"pre\",\"className\":\"language-text\"},mdx(\"span\",{parentName:\"code\",\"className\":\"line\"},mdx(\"span\",{parentName:\"span\"},`vault write auth/oidc/role/demo -\u003c\u003cEOF`)),`\n`,mdx(\"span\",{parentName:\"code\",\"className\":\"line\"},mdx(\"span\",{parentName:\"span\"},`{`)),`\n`,mdx(\"span\",{parentName:\"code\",\"className\":\"line\"},mdx(\"span\",{parentName:\"span\"},`  \"user_claim\": \"sub\",`)),`\n`,mdx(\"span\",{parentName:\"code\",\"className\":\"line\"},mdx(\"span\",{parentName:\"span\"},`  \"bound_audiences\": \"abc123\",`)),`\n`,mdx(\"span\",{parentName:\"code\",\"className\":\"line\"},mdx(\"span\",{parentName:\"span\"},`  \"role_type\": \"oidc\",`)),`\n`,mdx(\"span\",{parentName:\"code\",\"className\":\"line\"},mdx(\"span\",{parentName:\"span\"},`  \"policies\": \"demo\",`)),`\n`,mdx(\"span\",{parentName:\"code\",\"className\":\"line\"},mdx(\"span\",{parentName:\"span\"},`  \"ttl\": \"1h\",`)),`\n`,mdx(\"span\",{parentName:\"code\",\"className\":\"line\"},mdx(\"span\",{parentName:\"span\"},`  \"bound_claims\": { \"groups\": [\"mygroup/mysubgroup\"] }`)),`\n`,mdx(\"span\",{parentName:\"code\",\"className\":\"line\"},mdx(\"span\",{parentName:\"span\"},`}`)),`\n`,mdx(\"span\",{parentName:\"code\",\"className\":\"line\"},mdx(\"span\",{parentName:\"span\"},`EOF`)),`\n`)),mdx(\"ul\",null,mdx(\"li\",{parentName:\"ul\"},mdx(\"p\",{parentName:\"li\"},`Monitor Vault's log output. Important information about OIDC validation failures will be emitted.`)),mdx(\"li\",{parentName:\"ul\"},mdx(\"p\",{parentName:\"li\"},`Ensure Redirect URIs are correct in Vault and on the provider. They need to match exactly. Check:\nhttp/https, 127.0.0.1/localhost, port numbers, whether trailing slashes are present.`)),mdx(\"li\",{parentName:\"ul\"},mdx(\"p\",{parentName:\"li\"},`Start simple. The only claim configuration a role requires is `,mdx(\"inlineCode\",{parentName:\"p\"},`user_claim`),`. After authentication is\nknown to work, you can add additional claims bindings and metadata copying.`)),mdx(\"li\",{parentName:\"ul\"},mdx(\"a\",{parentName:\"li\",\"id\":\"bound_audiences\",\"className\":\"__target-lic\",\"aria-hidden\":\"true\"}),mdx(\"p\",{parentName:\"li\"},mdx(\"a\",{parentName:\"p\",\"href\":\"#bound_audiences\",\"aria-label\":\"bound_audiences permalink\",\"className\":\"__permalink-lic\"},mdx(\"inlineCode\",{parentName:\"a\"},`bound_audiences`)),` is optional for OIDC roles and typically not required. OIDC providers will use\nthe client_id as the audience and OIDC validation expects this.`)),mdx(\"li\",{parentName:\"ul\"},mdx(\"p\",{parentName:\"li\"},`Check your provider for what scopes are required in order to receive all\nof the information you need. The scopes \"profile\" and \"groups\" often need to be\nrequested, and can be added by setting `,mdx(\"inlineCode\",{parentName:\"p\"},`oidc_scopes=\"profile,groups\"`),` on the role.`)),mdx(\"li\",{parentName:\"ul\"},mdx(\"p\",{parentName:\"li\"},`If you're seeing claim-related errors in logs, review the provider's docs very carefully to see\nhow they're naming and structuring their claims. Depending on the provider, you may be able to\nconstruct a simple `,mdx(\"inlineCode\",{parentName:\"p\"},`curl`),` implicit grant request to obtain a JWT that you can inspect. An example\nof how to decode the JWT (in this case located in the \"access_token\" field of a JSON response):`),mdx(\"p\",{parentName:\"li\"},mdx(\"inlineCode\",{parentName:\"p\"},`cat jwt.json | jq -r .access_token | cut -d. -f2 | base64 -D`))),mdx(\"li\",{parentName:\"ul\"},mdx(\"p\",{parentName:\"li\"},`As of Vault 1.2, the `,mdx(\"a\",{parentName:\"p\",\"href\":\"/vault/api-docs/v1.21.x/auth/jwt#verbose_oidc_logging\"},mdx(\"inlineCode\",{parentName:\"a\"},`verbose_oidc_logging`)),` role\noption is available which will log the received OIDC token to the `,mdx(\"em\",{parentName:\"p\"},`server`),` logs if debug-level logging is enabled. This can\nbe helpful when debugging provider setup and verifying that the received claims are what you expect.\nSince claims data is logged verbatim and may contain sensitive information, this option should not be\nused in production.`)),mdx(\"li\",{parentName:\"ul\"},mdx(\"p\",{parentName:\"li\"},`Azure requires some additional configuration when a user is a member of more\nthan 200 groups, described in `,mdx(\"a\",{parentName:\"p\",\"href\":\"/vault/docs/v1.21.x/auth/jwt/oidc-providers/azuread#optional-azure-specific-configuration\"},`Azure-specific handling\nconfiguration`)))),mdx(\"h2\",{\"id\":\"jwt-authentication\"},mdx(\"a\",{parentName:\"h2\",\"className\":\"__permalink-h\",\"href\":\"#jwt-authentication\",\"aria-label\":\"jwt authentication permalink\"},`\\xbb`),`JWT authentication`),mdx(\"p\",null,`The authentication flow for roles of type \"jwt\" is simpler than OIDC since Vault\nonly needs to validate the provided JWT.`),mdx(\"h3\",{\"id\":\"jwt-verification\"},mdx(\"a\",{parentName:\"h3\",\"className\":\"__permalink-h\",\"href\":\"#jwt-verification\",\"aria-label\":\"jwt verification permalink\"},`\\xbb`),`JWT verification`),mdx(\"p\",null,`Vault verifies JWT signatures against public keys from the issuer. You can\nonly configure one JWT signature verification method per mounted backend from\nthe following options:`),mdx(\"ul\",null,mdx(\"li\",{parentName:\"ul\"},mdx(\"p\",{parentName:\"li\"},mdx(\"strong\",{parentName:\"p\"},`Static Keys`),`. A set of public keys is stored directly in the backend configuration. See the\n`,mdx(\"a\",{parentName:\"p\",\"href\":\"/vault/api-docs/v1.21.x/auth/jwt#jwt_validation_pubkeys\"},`jwt_validation_pubkeys`),`\nconfiguration option.`)),mdx(\"li\",{parentName:\"ul\"},mdx(\"p\",{parentName:\"li\"},mdx(\"strong\",{parentName:\"p\"},`JWKS`),`. A JSON Web Key Set (`,mdx(\"a\",{parentName:\"p\",\"href\":\"https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc7517\"},`JWKS`),`) URL and optional\ncertificate chain is configured. Keys will be fetched from this endpoint for authentication.\nSee the `,mdx(\"a\",{parentName:\"p\",\"href\":\"/vault/api-docs/v1.21.x/auth/jwt#jwks_url\"},`jwks_url`),` and `,mdx(\"a\",{parentName:\"p\",\"href\":\"/vault/api-docs/v1.21.x/auth/jwt#jwks_ca_pem\"},`jwks_ca_pem`),`\nconfiguration options.`)),mdx(\"li\",{parentName:\"ul\"},mdx(\"p\",{parentName:\"li\"},mdx(\"strong\",{parentName:\"p\"},`JWKS Pairs`),`. A list of JSON Web Key Set (`,mdx(\"a\",{parentName:\"p\",\"href\":\"https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc7517\"},`JWKS`),`) URLs and optional\ncertificate chain for each is configured. Keys will be fetched from each endpoint for authentication,\nstopping at the first set to successfully verify the JWT signature. See the\n`,mdx(\"a\",{parentName:\"p\",\"href\":\"/vault/api-docs/v1.21.x/auth/jwt#jwks_pairs\"},`jwks_pairs`),` configuration option.`)),mdx(\"li\",{parentName:\"ul\"},mdx(\"p\",{parentName:\"li\"},mdx(\"strong\",{parentName:\"p\"},`OIDC Discovery`),`. An OIDC Discovery URL and optional certificate chain is configured. Keys\nwill be fetched from this URL during authentication. When OIDC Discovery is used, OIDC validation\ncriteria (e.g. `,mdx(\"inlineCode\",{parentName:\"p\"},`iss`),`, `,mdx(\"inlineCode\",{parentName:\"p\"},`aud`),`, etc.) will be applied. See the `,mdx(\"a\",{parentName:\"p\",\"href\":\"/vault/api-docs/v1.21.x/auth/jwt#oidc_discovery_url\"},`oidc_discovery_url`),`\nand `,mdx(\"a\",{parentName:\"p\",\"href\":\"/vault/api-docs/v1.21.x/auth/jwt#oidc_discovery_ca_pem\"},`oidc_discovery_ca_pem`),` configuration\noptions.`))),mdx(\"p\",null,`To configure additional verification methods, you must mount and configure one\nbackend instance per method at different paths.`),mdx(\"p\",null,`After verifying the JWT signatures, Vault checks the corresponding `,mdx(\"inlineCode\",{parentName:\"p\"},`au